n><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fails_with_abbrev</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">mfderiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">product1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">τ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">fail_if_success</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">product1_smul_left</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">product1_smul_left</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- but rw works!</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fails_with_def</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">mfderiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">product2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">τ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">fail_if_success</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">product2_smul_left</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">product2_smul_left</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- but rw works!</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">works</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">product1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">τ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">product1_smul_left</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">works'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">product2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">τ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">product2_smul_left</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 595142623,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1778784101
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The key thing is we have an axiom saying <code>product1 R (f • σ) τ = f • product1 R σ τ</code>and somewhere we see <code>mfderiv E (product1 R (f • σ) τ) x = 0</code> and <code>simp</code> is not able to apply the axiom whereas <code>rw</code> is.</p>",
        "id": 595142843,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1778784166
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note there are two variants,  <code>product1</code> is a abbrev while <code>product2</code> is a def. In both cases <code>simp</code> fail when the products appear inside the <code>mfderiv</code> function but works on a bare one.</p>",
        "id": 595143123,
        "sender_full_name": "Patrick Massot",
        "timestamp": 1778784262
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note that it is also not possible to conv to the rewrite position to use <code>simp</code> there:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fails_with_abbrev</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">mfderiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">product1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">σ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">τ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">conv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">enter</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- `arg` conv tactic failed, cannot select argument</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I suspect that this failure has the same underlying reason.</p>",
        "id": 595276108,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1778842469
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>oh, that's because the type of <code>mfderiv E c x</code> depends on the value of <code>c</code></p>",
        "id": 595278167,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1778843183
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah, you're right. The problem is that the <code>c</code> in <code>mfderiv E c x</code> also appears in its type, so <code>c</code> is a dependent position. So, rewriting there may make the result type incorrect, because it changes the type, and only <code>dsimp</code> rewriting is supported.</p>",
        "id": 595279016,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1778843435
    }
]